;; A built-in hook (RFC-011, RFC-067 phase 2, byj-gly.460): in a literate
;; project the org file is the source, and a file org-babel tangled from it is
;; output. A write to such a file — known by org's link comments — is refused,
;; naming the org file to edit and tangle instead. Above the permission gate,
;; so the person is never asked about a write that would be refused anyway.
;; Off with :literate-guard? false.
{:id "tangled-file-guard"
 :event :agent.tool-use/pre
 :priority 87
 :on-error :throw
 :doc "Refuse write-file and update-file on a file org-babel tangled with link comments, naming the org file to edit and tangle instead."
 :impl :brainyard.literate/tangled-file-guard
 :opts {:tools #{"write-file" "update-file"}}}
